.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt BUSYBOX-PRINTUTILS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm busybox-printutils ,
.Nm lpd ,
.Nm lpq ,
.Nm lpr
.Nd BusyBox print tools
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm lpd
.Ar SPOOLDIR
.Op Ar HELPER Op Ar ARGS
.Nm lpq
.Op Fl P Ar queue Ns Op @ Ns Ar host Ns Op : Ns Ar port
.Op Fl U Ar USERNAME
.Op Fl d Ar JOBID
.Ar ...
.Op Fl fs
.Nm lpr
.Fl P Ar queue Ns Op @ Ns Ar host Ns Op : Ns Ar port
.Fl U Ar USERNAME
.Fl J Ar TITLE
.Fl Vmh
.Op Ar FILE
.Ar ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These are the printutils applets of BusyBox 1.36.1 as built for Rach2.
Rach2 has no printer.
.Bl -tag -width lpd
.It Nm lpd
Receive print jobs for queues in
.Ar SPOOLDIR .
That directory must contain device nodes, directories, or symbolic links
to them, with names matching the print queues.
Jobs for a device node are sent directly to the device.
Other jobs are stored in the queue directory and
.Ar HELPER
is called with the file name in the
.Ev DATAFILE
environment variable.
.It Nm lpq
Display or control queued print jobs.
.It Nm lpr
Submit files for printing.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
The following options apply to
.Nm lpq :
.Bl -tag -width "-U USERNAME"
.It Fl P Ar queue Ns Op @ Ns Ar host Ns Op : Ns Ar port
Select the print service.
Without this option, use
.Ev PRINTER .
.It Fl d Ar JOBID
Delete jobs.
.It Fl f
Force a waiting job to be printed.
.It Fl s
Use a short display.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
The BusyBox usage text gives this server command:
.Dl tcpsvd -E 0 515 softlimit -m 999999 lpd /var/spool ./print
.Sh HISTORY
